CM Template 3el Yagi-Uda for 20 meters @ 50 feet model 
CM Modified to be vertical element allowing tuning with Ht variable
CM 
CM Element Length Formulas
CM Reflector Length 0.475 to 0.5
CM (Typically ~5% longer than the driven element)
CM Driven Element Length 0.45 to 0.48
CM (Typically configured as a half-wave dipole, 
CM Director Lengths  0.40 to 0.44
CM (Each successive director is usually slightly shorter than the preceding one
CM 
CM Element Spacing Formulas
CM Reflector to Driven Element Spacing: 0.15 to 0.25 (commonly 0.2 to 0.25)
CM Driven Element to First Director Spacing: 0.10? to 0.15?
CM Director to Director Spacing: 0.10? to 0.30?
CM 
CM 
CM 
CM 
CE
SY freq = 14.2	'Frequency
SY ht = 15ft	'Mast mounted Height (feet)
SY rdis = 0.9114*2	'Reflector distance
SY ddis = 1.3716*2	'Director distance
SY rad = .005	'Radius of wire (diameter 1 cm) expressed as meter?
SY sol = 300000000	'Speed of light (rounded up)
SY Hz = freq * 100000	'Frequency variable in Hz
SY wavelength = sol / Hz	'Wavelength calc(lamda): Speed of light / frequency in Hz
SY dir_len = (wavelength * 0.44) / 2	'Director half-length: SOL / freq * 0.44
SY dr_len = (wavelength  * 0.47) / 2	'Driven element half-length: SOL / freq * 0.48
SY ref_len = (wavelength  * 0.05) / 2	'Reflector half-length: SOL / freq * 0.50
GW	1	19	ddis	0	ht+(dir_len/2)	ddis	0	ht-(dir_len/2)	rad	'Director
GW	2	19	0	0	ht+(dr_len/2)	0	0	ht-(dr_len/2)	rad	'Driven
GW	3	19	-rdis	0	ht+(ref_len/2)	-rdis	0	ht-(ref_len/2)	rad	'Reflector
GE	1
LD	5	1	0	0	24900000	'Alum. 6061-T6
LD	5	2	0	0	24900000
LD	5	3	0	0	24900000
GN	2	0	0	0	81	5.0
EK
EX	0	2	10	0	1	0	0
FR	0	0	0	0	freq	0
EN
